<!--
  The launcher mark: a Courier Prime Bold "P", extracted from the shipped
  CourierPrime-Bold.ttf rather than redrawn, so the icon is literally the brand's
  typeface instead of an approximation of it.

  Why a letterform and not the wordmark: PERSPECT1VE inside its rule is eleven
  tracked characters, illegible at 48dp. Why "P" and not the mirrored E that is
  the brand's signature move: an icon is seen without context hundreds of times,
  and its purpose is recognition. A lone reversed E risks reading as an error or
  as a 3 — cleverness that costs legibility fails the test the rest of the
  system is held to.

  Geometry: glyph cap height 46dp centred at (54,54) in the 108dp viewport, so it
  sits inside the 66dp safe zone with room on every side. The group flips Y
  (fonts grow upward, VectorDrawable downward) and scales 2048upm to dp in one
  transform — the path data below is the font's own coordinates, untouched.
-->
